  str_n18_1_name_desc_long = "You're woken from a sweet dream of winning the jackpot to huge bills and swarms of Eclipsites to deal with.",
  str_n18_2_name_desc_long = "Although Bethel's helping, the recruitment isn't going well. At your wit's end, the last three candidates come for the interview and give you hope. Nina, Sanae, and Minos suggest splitting into two teams to compete for the position.",
  str_n18_3_name_desc_long = "To wipe out Eclipsites, improve Cloud Gardens' management, and generate income to pay off debt, you go to the fertility plots where Unique Trees are growing. Three potential managers each show their special prowess. Nina also develops a keen interest in Chubbs, the fantastic residents of Cloud Gardens.",
  str_n18_4_name_desc_long = "Eclipsites come out of the woods. You and your allies make concerted efforts and defeat the enemy. Nina's true motives for wanting the job might be complicated, but her determination is beyond doubt. However, her rival Minos proves to be a very competitive caretaker.",
  str_n18_5_name_desc_long = "Following Eclipsite tracks, you and your companions reach the place where you and Vice once searched for treasures. Sanae finds some by luck, but this isn't enough to challenge Minos' leading edge. To win the bet, Nina heads off to look for tools but encounters Eclipsites in the warehouse.",
  str_n18_6_name_desc_long = "You have a chat with Nina and learn that she owns several stores in Umbraton. She seems hesitant when you ask about her achievement. But before you can get to the bottom of it, she distracts you with news of a Caelestite column in the Umbraton Daily.",
  str_n18_7_name_desc_long = "Nina shows a strong interest in the operations of Cloud Gardens, bringing your attention to some issues you never thought about before. Minos wins again, this time at mining, and earns the Chubbs' respect. After Sanae's puppet complains about the overwhelming workload, you decide to take a break.",
  str_n18_8_name_desc_long = "Everything is progressing smoothly, but you can't help worrying about Cloud Gardens. Nina suggests a fishing trip to lighten the mood. You fail to sell your unique fish-catching technique to Nina but find out why Nina ran away from home through Bethel and Minos' conversation. Some problems simply can't be solved with Nightium.",
  str_n18_9_name_desc_long = "Your room is enthusiastically cleaned by the potential managers as they're getting better and more professional, but Nina seems to have some trouble outside of work still. You comfort her with your own experiences, and she isn't against a heart-to-heart conversation with you. However, a new crisis is creeping in from the depths of the forest...",
  str_n18_10_name_desc_long = "The Eclipsite crisis is more serious than you expected. Unable to effectively solve the problem, you have no choice but to fight against them hand to hand. Hyacinth Tower becomes the only safe place in Cloud Gardens.",
  str_n18_11_name_desc_long = "Bethel is not yet back with mercenaries from Umbraton. You have to continuously fight with the Eclipsites. This seems to be the only way to defend your home based on your past experiences.",
  str_n18_12_name_desc_long = "In front of Fountain of Hope, Nina confesses all her troubles to you: the bet with Minos, her plans for Cloud Gardens, Umbraton, and her father... Inspired by Nina, you come up with a solution for this Eclipsite crisis—a very Caelestite solution.",
  str_n18_13_name_desc_long = "According to instructions from ancient Caelestite relics, your commands must be followed, your wishes brought to fruition. You know you must trust the Chubbs this time!",
